You are working on ContentForge, a full-stack TypeScript web application for creating and scheduling social media content about Data & AI topics.

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 3 + shadcn/ui (Radix primitives)
- Backend: Express.js 5 (Node.js)
- Database: PostgreSQL with Drizzle ORM 0.39
- AI: OpenAI gpt-4o-mini via Replit AI Integrations
- Routing: wouter 3.3 (frontend), Express (backend)
- State: TanStack React Query v5
- Rich Text: TipTap 3
- Charts: Recharts 2

## Architecture
Monolithic client-server app. Express serves both API routes (/api/*) and the Vite-built React frontend on port 5000.

Key files:
- `shared/schema.ts` — ALL data types (Drizzle schema + Zod insert schemas + TS types)
- `server/routes.ts` — ALL API endpoints (~1867 lines)
- `server/storage.ts` — IStorage interface + DatabaseStorage implementation
- `server/db.ts` — PostgreSQL connection
- `client/src/App.tsx` — Root component with routing and sidebar layout
- `client/src/lib/queryClient.ts` — TanStack Query config and apiRequest helper
- `client/src/lib/constants.ts` — Content pillars, post types, tones, platforms

## Critical Rules

### Data Model
- Define ALL types in `shared/schema.ts` using Drizzle ORM
- Export insert schemas via `createInsertSchema(table).omit({ id: true, createdAt: true })`
- Export select types via `typeof table.$inferSelect`
- Use `text().array()` for array columns (NOT `array(text())`)
- NEVER change primary key column types (serial ↔ varchar)

### Backend
- Validate ALL request bodies with Zod before passing to storage
- Keep routes thin — business logic goes in storage methods
- Every AI call must use `aiCall()` helper and be followed by `logAiUsage()`
- Use `safeJsonParse()` for AI JSON responses
- Token/secrets: NEVER return unmasked tokens in API responses

### Frontend
- TanStack Query v5 object form only: `useQuery({ queryKey: ['/api/posts'] })`
- Default queryFn is configured — queries don't need their own fetch function
- Mutations use `apiRequest(method, url, data)` then `queryClient.invalidateQueries()`
- Forms use `react-hook-form` + `zodResolver` + shadcn Form component
- No explicit React import (Vite JSX transform)
- Use `import.meta.env.VITE_*` for frontend env vars
- Add `data-testid` to all interactive and meaningful display elements

### Styling
- Tailwind utility classes with shadcn/ui components
- Dark mode via CSS variables — always provide light/dark variants
- Icons: `lucide-react` for actions, `react-icons/si` for brand logos
- Colors use HSL format in CSS vars: `--my-var: 23 10% 23%`

### Storage Pattern
```typescript
// 1. Add method to IStorage interface
// 2. Implement in DatabaseStorage class
// 3. Use in routes via `storage.methodName()`
```

### Do NOT Modify
- `vite.config.ts`, `server/vite.ts`, `drizzle.config.ts` — pre-configured
- `package.json` scripts — ask before changing
- Primary key column types in schema

### After Schema Changes
Run `npm run db:push` to sync with database.

## Content Domain
6 content pillars: Data Infrastructure & MLOps, AI for DevOps/AIOps, Cloud-Native Data Platforms, Infrastructure as Code for Data, Career & Leadership, Hot Takes & Trends.
Post types: tweet, thread, hot_take, poll, quote_template.
Statuses: draft, ready, scheduled, posted, failed.
Platforms: x, threads, both.
